#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD1361 expect=skipped domain=DM
#note "THE ALL-FACET GATE, NEW WITH THE R-5.25 SPLIT (top-level-or board wave 1, \u00a74). The parent's half keeps a bare empty(ARMCD) leaf, so on a DM without the ARMCD column every ARM-populated row would fire; the rule carried NO Requirements before the split and DID flood here. Requirements.Variables.All [ARMCD, ARM] now rejects the dataset, SKIPPED naming the variable - ruling in documentation/derivation/absent-column-verdicts.tsv (verdict 2-2). Twin fixture: PMDA-SD1361-skipped_armcd_column_absent, which carries the Fix #331 history. If this scenario EXECUTES, the gate has been removed: escalate, do not rewrite the pin."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset DM class="SPECIAL PURPOSE" label="Demographics"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col ARM     type=Char label="Description of Planned Arm"
---
S1 | DM | 001 | Treatment A
